{
  "name": "inbox-det (the To review screen, default and developer mode; nothing waits at cold boot, so the one list is provoked through stubInvoke on list_pending_decisions)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "The decisions waiting for the user live in memory (the consents of a conversation, the questions) or need a paused task or a batch, none of which a seed can write, so the list is provoked through stubInvoke on list_pending_decisions. The value imitates the backend type PendingDecisionList (items of PendingDecision, crates/apollia-runtime/src/api/routes_pending.rs): one consent, one consent on code, one question, one batch item, one paused task.",
    "decide_pending_decision is stubbed for the whole block and imitates DecideResponse with batchItemsResumed 1: an answer given on a stubbed item names an id the runtime does not hold, and the real call would answer UNKNOWN_ITEM. The stub is sticky because leaving the screen sends every held answer at once.",
    "An answer is held about six seconds before it is sent, which is what Cancel takes back: review-answered appears at once, review-resumed only after the hold ran out and the stubbed answer came back. The stubbed list is static, so the answered item is listed again after its answer settled.",
    "The developer mode swaps the decision card for the developer card of the chat (approval-card-<tool>, with its full arguments behind approval-see-more-<tool>); the default mode shows operator-approval-<tool>."
  ],
  "dynamicTestids": [
    "approval-card-file_write",
    "approval-detail-file_write",
    "approval-see-more-file_write",
    "operator-approval-accept-bash_executor",
    "operator-approval-accept-file_write",
    "operator-approval-always-bash_executor",
    "operator-approval-always-file_write",
    "operator-approval-always-send_email",
    "operator-approval-code-bash_executor",
    "operator-approval-refuse-bash_executor",
    "review-filter-all",
    "review-filter-batch_items",
    "review-filter-decisions",
    "review-filter-questions",
    "review-question-other-figure",
    "review-question-radio-figure-ledger",
    "settings-nav-developer"
  ],
